hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"265","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadafi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa told me Ibn Al-Zubair, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I never understood my parents unless they practiced the religion, and it did not pass on to us. A day when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will come to us at both ends of the day, morning and evening. He mentioned the hadith in its length, and he said in the report: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I have been shown the place of your migration. I have been shown a marsh with palm trees between two palm trees, which are Al-Hartan,” so he mentioned the hadith. For his heroism in the migration of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mecca to Medina. Abu Bakr said: In the words of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I was shown a marsh with palm trees between two palm trees,” and his informing them that it was a house Their migration, and that of the entire city, was an indication that the entire city was a marsh, even if dry ablution was not permissible in a marsh. The marshland was as some of the people of our time imagined, that it was from an evil land, as He said: And he who is evil does not come out except in distress. Surat Al-A’raf, verse 58, the basis for this article would be that the land of the city is bad and not good, and this is the statement of some stubborn people, when they criticized the people of The city, and he said: It is evil, so know that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called it Tayyibah or Taybah, for the marshy land is good, according to what The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported that the city is good, and if it is good and it is a marsh, then God Almighty has commanded tayammum. With the good plain in the text of his book, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew that the city was good or good, while he informed them that it was A marsh, and from this it is clear and proven that tayammum using a marsh is permissible."
